          "distinct": false,
          "id": "14af86e79b688b81b84bd26b246e541df3b53b64",
          "message": "[pdata/pprofile] Use dictionary references over gRPC (#16016)\n\n<!--Ex. Fixing a bug - Describe the bug and how this fixes the issue.\nEx. Adding a feature - Explain what this achieves.-->\n#### Description\n\nThe OTLP/gRPC Profiles client was sending the raw profiles payload\nwithout converting resource and scope attributes into references to the\n`ProfilesDictionary`. This made the gRPC path inconsistent with the\nexpected Profiles wire representation.\n\nThis change performs the dictionary conversion in `pprofileotlp` before\nthe request is sent, while preserving the read-only semantics of the\ninput by operating on a copy. On the receiving side, dictionary\nreferences are resolved before attributes are exposed to pdata\nconsumers.\n\nThe implementation does not introduce an additional\nserialization/deserialization round trip.\n\n<!-- Issue number if applicable -->\n#### Link to tracking issue\n\nFixes #15861\n\n<!--Describe what testing was performed and which tests were added.-->\n#### Testing\n\nAdded and ran unit and end-to-end gRPC tests covering:\n\n* ProfilesDictionary references in the serialized gRPC payload\n* resource attributes\n* scope attributes\n* resolution of dictionary references on the receiving side\n* preservation of mutable and read-only input data on both successful\nand failed RPCs\n\nAlso ran the relevant pdata/pprofile tests, race tests, `golangci-lint`,\n`gofmt`, `goimports`, `gofumpt`, and `git diff --check`.\n\n<!--Describe the documentation added.-->\n#### Documentation\n\nAdded a changelog entry. No additional user-facing documentation is\nrequired, since this fixes the OTLP/gRPC Profiles wire representation\nwithout introducing a user-visible configuration.\n\n<!--Authorship attestation. See AGENTS.md for details. AI agents must\nnot check this box on behalf\nof the user; the human author must check it themselves before the PR is\nready for review.-->\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\n<!--Please delete paragraphs that you did not use before submitting.-->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Damien Mathieu <42@dmathieu.com>",
