          "id": "112c28884bdf926f63568ef96abf5b520db98b6e",
          "message": "[chore][cmd/mdatagen] Remove non-deterministic test from generated output (#16200)\n\n<!--Ex. Fixing a bug - Describe the bug and how this fixes the issue.\nEx. Adding a feature - Explain what this achieves.-->\n#### Description\n\nmdatagen's generated `generated_config_test.go` used to include a\n`TestConfigValidate_DefaultValid` (and `Test<Type>Validate_DefaultValid`\nfor named `exported_configs` types) test, asserting that a\ndefault/zero-value-constructed config passes `Validate()`.\n\nThis test has been removed. mdatagen cannot deterministically know, at\ngeneration time, whether a default or zero value will satisfy a\ncomponent's `Validate()` — in particular, `custom_validator` logic is\nopaque to the generator, so the only way to know if a default is \"valid\"\nis to actually run the real validator.\n\nThe atomic, per-rule failure-case tests (required fields, numeric\nbounds, enum values) are unaffected — those remain deterministic and are\nstill generated.\n\n<!--Authorship attestation. See AGENTS.md for details. AI agents must\nnot check this box on behalf\nof the user; the human author must check it themselves before the PR is\nready for review.-->\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\n<!--Please delete paragraphs that you did not use before submitting.-->",
