          "id": "6d99d817efd3a1bbc155beb1027a68fcce9da4d6",
          "message": "[otlphttpexporter]report the resolved URL in HTTP status errors (#16215)\n\n<!--Ex. Fixing a bug - Describe the bug and how this fixes the issue.\nEx. Adding a feature - Explain what this achieves.-->\n#### Description\n\nMiddleware `RoundTripper` clones the request before rewriting its URL.\nThe exporter's own `req.URL` keeps the configured placeholder, so\n4xx/5xx error messages report a host the request never went to.\n\n#14680 fixed this for transport errors by overriding `url.Error.URL`\nwith `req.URL`, which only helps when the middleware mutates the request\nin place.\n\n`http.Transport` sets `resp.Request` to the request it actually sent,\nincluding the rewritten URL. The PR reads the destination from there,\nfalling back to the configured URL when absent.\n\n<!-- Issue number if applicable -->\n#### Link to tracking issue\nFixes #14673 (the missing bit)\n\n<!--Describe what testing was performed and which tests were added.-->\n#### Testing\n\nUnit tests added\n\n<!--Describe the documentation added.-->\n#### Documentation\nN/A\n<!--Authorship attestation. See AGENTS.md for details. AI agents must\nnot check this box on behalf\nof the user; the human author must check it themselves before the PR is\nready for review.-->\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\n<!--Please delete paragraphs that you did not use before submitting.-->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alex Boten <223565+codeboten@users.noreply.github.com>",
