          "distinct": false,
          "id": "d93a9edb22c1af6bd1fdbe2cfdd432a25f6e1e62",
          "message": "Update module google.golang.org/grpc to v1.85.0 (#16240)\n\nThis PR contains the following updates:\n\n| Package | Change |\n[Age](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n[Confidence](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [google.golang.org/grpc](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go) |\n`v1.84.0` → `v1.85.0` |\n![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/go/google.golang.org%2fgrpc/v1.85.0?slim=true)\n|\n![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/go/google.golang.org%2fgrpc/v1.84.0/v1.85.0?slim=true)\n|\n\n---\n\n### Release Notes\n\n<details>\n<summary>grpc/grpc-go (google.golang.org/grpc)</summary>\n\n###\n[`v1.85.0`](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/releases/tag/v1.85.0):\nRelease 1.85.0\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/compare/v1.84.0...v1.85.0)\n\n### New Features\n\n- stats: Expose the effective client authority (sent on the wire as the\nHTTP/2 `:authority` header) in client `stats.OutHeader` events.\n([#&#8203;9296](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9296))\n- Special Thanks: [@&#8203;aryansk](https://redirect.github.com/aryansk)\n- metadata: Add `ValueFromOutgoingContext`, which reads a single\nmetadata value from outgoing context without copying the entire outgoing\nmetadata into a new map.\n([#&#8203;9282](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9282))\n- Special Thanks:\n[@&#8203;yuyangguo42](https://redirect.github.com/yuyangguo42)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- transport: Refine control buffer throttling to only count peer-induced\ncontrol frames, raise the default\n`GRPC_GO_EXPERIMENTAL_CONTROL_BUFFER_THROTTLE_LIMIT` from 100 to 10,000,\nand close client connections if reads remain throttled for `10s`.\n([#&#8203;9563](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9563))\n- server: Ensure `Stop()` forcefully terminates the server while\n`GracefulStop()` is waiting for active handlers to complete.\n([#&#8203;9394](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9394))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;stanhu](https://redirect.github.com/stanhu)\n- server: Unconditionally increment the highest-seen stream ID on when\nhandling `HEADERS` frames to comply with [RFC 7540\n§5.1.1](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7540.html#section-5.1.1).\nPreviously, truncated `HEADERS` frames left the connection in an\ninconsistent state and allowed stream IDs to be reused by clients\nwithout resulting in a protocol error.\n([#&#8203;9414](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9414))\n- server: Terminate streams immediately when a `HEADERS` frame includes\nthe `EndStream` bit. Previously, this caused server handlers to hang\nwhen reading a message.\n([#&#8203;9391](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9391))\n- server: Reject requests missing both `:authority` and `Host` headers\nwith HTTP 400 and status `Internal`.\n([#&#8203;9365](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9365))\n- xds: Fix a bug where route header matchers with non-lowercase names\nfailed to match routes.\n([#&#8203;9353](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9353))\n- Special Thanks:\n[@&#8203;winklemad](https://redirect.github.com/winklemad)\n- client: Ensure retried RPCs use the correct `:authority` value\nspecified by the LB policy instead of inheriting it from a previous\nattempt.\n([#&#8203;9277](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9277))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- transport: Fail streams with `io.ErrUnexpectedEOF` instead of `io.EOF`\nupon receiving truncated message headers or bodies after partial data\nhas already been received.\n([#&#8203;9204](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9204))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;buger](https://redirect.github.com/buger)\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Configuration\n\n📅 **Schedule**: (UTC)\n\n- Branch creation\n  - \"on tuesday\"\n- Automerge\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n\n🚦 **Automerge**: Disabled by config. Please merge this manually once you\nare satisfied.\n\n♻ **Rebasing**: Whenever PR becomes conflicted, or you tick the\nrebase/retry checkbox.\n\n🔕 **Ignore**: Close this PR and you won't be reminded about this update\nagain.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] <!-- rebase-check -->If you want to rebase/retry this PR, check\nthis box\n\n---\n\nThis PR was generated by [Mend Renovate](https://mend.io/renovate/).\nView the [repository job\nlog](https://developer.mend.io/github/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector).\n\n<!--renovate-debug:eyJjcmVhdGVkSW5WZXIiOiI0NC4xODQuMSIsInVwZGF0ZWRJblZlciI6IjQ0LjE4NC4xIiwidGFyZ2V0QnJhbmNoIjoibWFpbiIsImxhYmVscyI6WyJkZXBlbmRlbmNpZXMiLCJyZW5vdmF0ZWJvdCJdfQ==-->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: otelbot <197425009+otelbot@users.noreply.github.com>",
