          "distinct": true,
          "id": "adbedb4fd801bee1dfc20f06bdaf845239145478",
          "message": "[exporterhelper] Fix ref/unref imbalance in the sending queue (#16248)\n\n#### Description\n\nThe async queue released a reference for every request it read,\nincluding ones the persistent queue\nhad just deserialized and never took a reference for. When such a\nrequest is forwarded into another\npipeline, the refconsumer at that boundary adopts and releases it, and\nthe queue's extra release\nunderflows the reference count and panics with `Cannot unref freed\ndata`.\n\nOnly the in-memory queue keeps the request itself, so it is now the only\none that takes a reference.\nIt releases it once the request is reported as done rather than when the\nconsumer returns, which was\ntoo early: a batcher keeps the `Done` of every request it merged until\nthe resulting batch is sent.\n\nSupersedes #15739, whose end-to-end test is reused here.\n\n#### Link to tracking issue\n\nFixes #15256\n\n#### Testing\n\n`internal/e2e/persistent_queue_test.go` reproduces the panic with a\nconnector whose persistent\nsending queue forwards into a second pipeline.\n`TestAsyncMemoryQueueReleasesReferenceOnDone` covers\nthe release point, and\n`TestAsyncMemoryWaitForResultQueueReleasesReferenceOnDone` covers that\n`wait_for_result` does not change who owns the reference.\n\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-28T21:32:02Z",
          "tree_id": "5c927a3d36013aa359e0408f8d847db6a9c83cb4",
