          "distinct": false,
          "id": "c3c4fed36c388439be2533d9d712b1879774105b",
          "message": "[chore] Run unit tests with GODEBUG=fips140=only again (#16259)\n\n#### Description\nReverts #14571. The test target runs with `GODEBUG=fips140=only` again,\nas it did before the Go 1.26 bump.\n\nThat prefix was dropped because Go 1.26.0 and 1.26.1 could not complete\na TLS handshake in that mode (golang/go#78178) which broke module\ndownloads during the tests. The fix was shipped in Go 1.26.3.\n\nAfter adding `GODEBUG=fips140=only`, one test still failed:\nscraper/scraperhelper/internal/controller panicked with:\n```\nfips140/drbg: failed to obtain initial entropy\n```\n\nThat is not a crypto violation. The failure reason is that\n`receivertest.NewNopSettings` generates a UUID with `crypto/rand`. Go\n1.26 the FIPS DRBG panics the first time it is seeded inside a synctest\nbubble because the bubble's clock is frozen (golang/go#78557, fixed in\nGo 1.27).\n\n<!-- Issue number if applicable -->\n#### Link to tracking issue\nRelates to #\n\n<!--Describe what testing was performed and which tests were added.-->\n#### Testing\n- Run locally\n\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\nSigned-off-by: Israel Blancas <iblancasa@gmail.com>",
