          "distinct": false,
          "id": "3d2f065bbe16e5b18e7d9aa192b5a0c428464a77",
          "message": "[chore][cmd/mdatagen] Make config default constructors private inside component packages (#16264)\n\n<!--Ex. Fixing a bug - Describe the bug and how this fixes the issue.\nEx. Adding a feature - Explain what this achieves.-->\n#### Description\n\nComponent `Config` types already follow an established-but-undocumented\nconvention: the factory-wiring function (`createDefaultConfig`) is\nunexported, even though the `Config` type it returns is public - because\nit's only ever invoked as a function value passed into\n`NewFactory(...)`, never called directly by consumers. Nested config\ntypes inside the same component package didn't follow that convention —\ntheir `NewDefault<Type>()` constructors were exported, even though\nnothing outside the package can or should call them directly.\n\nThis change extends the existing privacy convention down to those nested\ntypes: inside a component package\n(receiver/exporter/processor/connector/extension/scraper — anything not\nin mdatagen's nonComponents list), locally-defined default constructors\nare now generated as `newDefault<Type>()` (unexported). Constructors for\nexternally-referenced types, and all constructors in non-component\npackages are unaffected and stay exported.\n\nIdea for this change came up as a result of discussion in #16212.\n\n<!--Describe what testing was performed and which tests were added.-->\n#### Testing\n\n- Regenerated samplescraper's fixtures\n- Update unit tests\n\n<!--Authorship attestation. See AGENTS.md for details. AI agents must\nnot check this box on behalf\nof the user; the human author must check it themselves before the PR is\nready for review.-->\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\n<!--Please delete paragraphs that you did not use before submitting.-->",
